"Steam Rankine Cycle — 60 MW Power Plant

In a 60 MW steam power plant, steam enters the turbine at 70 bar and 500 C.
Given data:
  - Condenser pressure: 0.1 bar
  - Boiler pressure drop: approx. 4 bar
  - Overall boiler efficiency: 0.90
  - Condenser cooling water temperature rise: limited to 10 C
  - Isentropic efficiency of turbine: 0.85
  - Alternator efficiency: 0.95
  - Isentropic efficiency of pumps and drive motor efficiency: 0.85 and 0.94 respectively

Determine:
  - Steam flow rate
  - Boiler power
  - Plant thermal efficiency
  - Condenser cooling water flow rate
"

W_dot_el=60E6 "[W]"
p_cd=0.1E5 "[Pa]"
DELTA_p=4E5 "[Pa]"
eta_boiler=0.9
DELTAT_w_cd=10
epsilon_s_t=0.85
eta_a=0.95
epsilon_s_p=0.85
eta_m=0.94

"POINT 1: condenser outlet:"
x_1=0
h_1=enthalpy(water,P=P_cd,x=x_1)
s_1=entropy(water,P=P_cd,x=x_1)

"POINT 2: pump outlet"
epsilon_s_p=(h_2_s-h_1)/(h_2-h_1)
h_2_s=enthalpy(water,s=s_1,P=P_2)
P_2=P_3+DELTA_P
P_3=70E5

"POINT 3: boiler outlet = turbine inlet"
T_3=500 "[°C]"
h_3=enthalpy(water,P=P_3,T=T_3)
s_3=entropy(water,P=P_3,T=T_3)

"POINT 4: turbine outlet"
epsilon_s_t=(h_3-h_4)/(h_3-h_4_s)
h_4_s=enthalpy(water,s=s_3,P=P_cd)
x_4=quality(water,P=P_cd,h=h_4)

"PLANT POWER:"
W_dot_el=W_dot_t*eta_a
W_dot_t=M_dot_steam*(h_3-h_4)

"BOILER"
Q_dot_boiler=M_dot_steam*(h_3-h_2)/eta_boiler

"PUMP WORK"
W_dot_p=M_dot_steam*(h_2-h_1)/eta_m

"THERMAL EFFICIENCY"
eta=W_dot_el/(Q_dot_boiler+W_dot_p)

"CONDENSER COOLING WATER FLOW RATE"
Q_dot_cd=M_dot_steam*(h_4-h_1)
Q_dot_cd=M_dot_w_cd*cp_w*DELTAT_w_cd
cp_w=4186